<com:TContent ID="body" >

<h1>TStyleSheet</h1>
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.WebControls.TStyleSheet" />
<p class="block-content">
<tt>TStyleSheet</tt> links a CSS file to the page, imports a CSS library bundled with PRADO,
or carries a block of CSS code. It is the stylesheet counterpart of
<a href="?page=Controls.ClientScript">TClientScript</a>.
</p>

<h2>Linking a Stylesheet File</h2>
<p class="block-content">
The <tt>StyleSheetUrl</tt> property names the CSS file to link. The property value is a
<a href="?page=Configurations.Templates3">dynamic asset tag</a>, so a file relative to the
current template is published to the assets directory automatically.
</p>
<com:TTextHighlighter Language="prado" CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TStyleSheet StyleSheetUrl=&lt;%~ style.css %&gt; /&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>
<p class="block-content">
A full URL string links a stylesheet from another server. When only a file URL is specified,
you may place the control anywhere on the page, and the <tt>&lt;link&gt;</tt> element renders
in the correct position.
</p>

<h2>Restricting the Media Type</h2>
<p class="block-content">
The <tt>MediaType</tt> property sets the media the stylesheet applies to, such as
<tt>print</tt> or <tt>screen</tt>. An empty value applies the stylesheet to all media types.
</p>
<com:TTextHighlighter Language="prado" CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TStyleSheet StyleSheetUrl=&lt;%~ print.css %&gt; MediaType="print" /&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<com:SinceVersion Version="3.3.1" />
<h2>Importing Bundled CSS Libraries</h2>
<p class="block-content">
The <tt>PradoStyles</tt> property imports a CSS library bundled with PRADO. Multiple libraries
are specified as a comma delimited string. The following example imports the jQuery UI dialog
and progressbar styles.
</p>
<com:TTextHighlighter Language="prado" CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TStyleSheet PradoStyles="jquery.ui.dialog, jquery.ui.progressbar" /&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>
<p class="block-content">
The supported libraries are <tt>jquery-ui</tt> and the individual
<tt>jquery.ui.<i>componentname</i></tt> libraries.
</p>

<h2>Including a CSS Code Block</h2>
<p class="block-content">
Any content inside the <tt>TStyleSheet</tt> control tag is treated as CSS code and renders
within a <tt>&lt;style&gt;</tt> element. Place the control in the <tt>&lt;head&gt;</tt> section
of the page when it carries a code block, so the output conforms to the HTML standard.
</p>
<com:TTextHighlighter Language="prado" CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TStyleSheet&gt;
  .highlight { background-color: yellow; }
&lt;/com:TStyleSheet&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

</com:TContent>
